# .worktreesync — declarative untracked-state sync, read by `wt-sync` from the
# SOURCE (main) worktree. Copy this file to `.worktreesync` in your repo root
# and commit it, so every worktree of the repo gets the same treatment.
#
# Format:  <mode> <path>
#
# Modes:
#   copy    one-time copy when missing in the target; never overwrites, so a
#           worktree can diverge freely after it is created
#   clone   block-sharing tree clone when the target is missing or empty —
#           APFS clonefile on macOS, hardlinks elsewhere. For big generated
#           directories where a plain copy is slow and doubles disk usage.
#   link    symlink target -> source, so state is shared both ways and
#           survives worktree deletion. Refuses to clobber a diverged file.
#
# Path matching:
#   .env          no slash   -> depth pattern: matches ignored paths only
#                              (per `git ls-files --others --ignored
#                              --exclude-standard`) whose basename is `.env`,
#                              at any depth. An untracked-but-not-gitignored
#                              `.env` will NOT match; wt-sync logs
#                              "skip .env (no matches)" for it.
#   /.env         leading /  -> root-anchored literal: the root .env only
#   src/app/.env  other /    -> literal repo-relative path
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

# Big generated trees — cloned, so a new worktree costs almost no extra disk.
clone node_modules
clone .venv

# Secrets and local config — copied once, then yours to diverge.
copy .env
copy .env.local

# Shared state you want to edit in exactly one place.
link .claude/settings.local.json
